// Copy to Config/Local.xcconfig (gitignored) to sign a Debug build for your own iPhone (README "Run it on your iPhone").
//
// Default: the paid DrivePerf team (Apple Developer Program, DRIVE-42). The Debug build signs as com.driveperf.app.dev,
// its widget extension as com.driveperf.app.dev.widgets, both with the App Group group.com.driveperf.app. Those IDs and
// the group are registered in that team's portal. Set DEVELOPMENT_TEAM to its Team ID (developer.apple.com/account ›
// Membership details). Release builds ignore this team on purpose: the release lane signs com.driveperf.app.
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = YOURTEAMID
CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Automatic
CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = Apple Development

// Fallback, a free Personal Team (no access to the paid team, or the membership has lapsed): set DEVELOPMENT_TEAM above
// to the Personal Team's ID and uncomment all three lines below. They go together. The bundle ID override keeps the
// Personal Team away from com.driveperf.*, which it could claim and block for the paid team. A free team cannot use
// App Groups, so the two entitlement lines swap in variants without the group: the widget and the Control Center
// control then show their empty state and the app skips publishing the widget snapshot.
// DP_APP_ID_DEBUG = com.yourname.driveperf.dev
// DP_ENTITLEMENTS_APP = Config/DrivePerf.personal-team.entitlements
// DP_ENTITLEMENTS_WIDGETS = Config/DrivePerfWidgets.personal-team.entitlements
